+ *   excursions on a composing link. (The earlier "HS: no effect" dead end
+ *   was measured on a static screen, against the dropped-write bug.)
+ *
+ * bl_double: send the packet twice. The first DCS write on an idle link is
+ *   consumed as a wake-up (measured); this is the static-set correctness
+ *   workaround, kept separate so it never confounds the drag tests.
+ *
+ * init_df / init_no_e7: vendor-init parity, applied on the next panel
+ *   re-init (power-button blank/unblank). The vendor on-command sends
+ *   df 0a 70 between the two b0 writes and contains no 0xe7 writes at all;
+ *   ours skips the former and adds two 18-byte 0xe7s of unknown origin.
+ *   A DDIC configured off-spec may be exactly the one that cannot take a
+ *   runtime DCS write mid-composition.
