+/*
+ * Post-corruption autopsy: writing a register number here performs one DCS
+ * read and logs the result. Separates "DDIC dead on the bus" (read times
+ * out, like the t=79s Invalid-response cluster) from "DDIC alive but the
+ * decoder is desynced" (0x0A still answers 0x9c under full-screen noise).
+ * DCS reads collide with frame traffic -- only use it on a static screen,
+ * and read ONE register per write (back-to-back reads desynchronise).
+ */
